{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftsyFz74pT5Ktz4CNLKG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0156UxTJV9zvzThS7zNny4QD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-886\\docs\\reviews\\wi-886\\001-ADJUDICATE-dc07129.md","content":"# WI-886 Done-when adjudication: WI-847's in-lane edit, 001 at dc07129\n\nSubject: WI-847 (`docs/archive/work/complete/WI-847-loop-reviewer-resumes-in-lane.md`). I compared the Done-when claimed at ab1c858d88 with the current one. The purpose, as WI-847's Context states it, now includes the owner's ruling of 2026-10-10 (D-008): \"This row lands step 1, the narrow round's brief rendered through the one reviewer render. Reviewer retention and the merge gate's freshness binding move to their own row.\"\n\n- [MOVED] \"The loop's REVIEW role can resume its session within one lane's review chain...\" (dropped) -> the lane owed reviewer retention through keep, store and lease, behind its own dial, shipped off -> it owes none -> not the same: a whole capability left the row. BLESSED as a move, because the owner moved it (D-008) and it is carried forward rather than lost: WI-887 (queued) owes \"the loop's REVIEW role can resume its session within one lane's iteration, through the keep operation, the store and the lease ... The dial ships off.\"\n- [MOVED] \"The review that gates a merge is always a fresh session over the full lane (claim base to tip)...\" (dropped) -> the lane owed the gate's freshness binding -> it owes none -> not the same. BLESSED as a move: WI-884 (queued) owes \"the merge-gating round is a fresh session over the full lane, from the recorded claim base to the tip\", plus the three gate hazards found while building it. WI-887 owes that the final reviewer never resumes an iteration reviewer's session.\n- [MOVED] \"Tests: two iteration rounds resume one session; the merge-gating round mints fresh...; dial off changes nothing.\" (dropped) -> the lane owed those three tests -> it owes none of them -> not the same. BLESSED as a move: WI-887's tests carry \"two iteration rounds resume one session\", \"the gating round in fresh mode mints fresh\" and \"with the dial off, nothing changes\"; WI-884's tests carry the gate's full-lane range.\n- [MOVED] \"The narrow round's reading scope ... is a render of `prompts/reviewer.template.md` through `prompts.py`, the same render the coordinator's reviews use.\" (rewritten) -> the narrow scope is rendered through the one reviewer render -> the same, PLUS \"one home for the narrow range sentence\" -> not the same: widened by one obligation. A close with a duplicated range sentence would pass the old item and fail the new. BLESSED: it is the same work made stricter. The landed code has `agent_brief.narrow_scope_line` as that one home, shared by the attended `review_brief` render, which WI-847's sitting 001 verified.\n- [MOVED] \"SR-227 amended to cover the review class, or a new SR...\" (dropped) -> the lane owed a spine change for retention -> it owes none -> not the same. BLESSED as a move: the retention class went with WI-887, which owes \"SR-227 amended to cover the review class and the final reviewer's configuration, or a new SR\". Step 1 never touched SR-227's subject.\n- [MOVED] \"The narrow round's reading scope ... with one home for the narrow range sentence.\" (added) -> nothing claimed beyond the rewritten item -> the render plus the single home for the range sentence -> not the same; this is the added half of the rewrite above. BLESSED, for the reason given there.\n- [MOVED] \"A template override that cannot carry the slots refuses the render.\" (added) -> nothing -> an override missing a slot refuses rather than rendering a full-lane or holed scope -> not the same: a new obligation. BLESSED: it is the refusal half of rendering \"through `prompts.py`\" (a strict fill), and the purpose is served better by refusing than by sending a wrong reading scope.\n- [MOVED] \"Tests: the loop's narrow render carries the delta and the attended render's range sentence; an override without the slots refuses.\" (added) -> no tests named for the narrow render -> two tests -> not the same: new verification owed. BLESSED: these are the tests step 1 needs, and `test_the_loop_narrow_round_renders_its_delta_through_the_one_render` and `test_a_loop_narrow_round_refuses_an_override_that_cannot_carry_its_range` hold them.\n- [MOVED] \"The rows the change makes untrue or incomplete (LLR-045, TC-082) state it and pass adjudication on the one adjudication path.\" (added) -> the claim's spine item named SR-227 for the retention class -> the rows owed are now LLR-045 and TC-082, the narrow render's chain under SR-154 -> not the same: different rows. BLESSED: they are the rows step 1 changes. WI-847's sitting 001 judged them MEANING and blessed them, and they were re-attested in act 92.\n\nAll nine changes move the scope, and I bless every move. What moves away is no longer part of WI-847's stated purpose: its Context records the owner's split, which narrows the row to step 1, and nothing the claim owed is lost. Every dropped obligation is carried by a queued row on trunk: WI-884 (narrow-round wiring and the fresh full-lane gate binding) and WI-887 (REVIEW retention, the configurable final reviewer, and SR-227). Those rows came out of the owner's D-008 and the coordinator's D-012 after WI-884's scope critique. Drafting successors here would mint duplicates of them. What was added is step 1 made stricter: one home for the range sentence, a strict refusal, and named tests.\n\nDONE-WHEN: BLESSED changes=9 digest=sha256:ea8462b50c12fe15\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1737,"cache_read_input_tokens":315300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1737},"output_tokens":8,"service